// petri.config — demo throttle to make the QUEUED state visible.
//
// Why this exists:
//   On the local executor, Nextflow moves a task from `process_submitted`
//   (QUEUED) to `process_started` (RUNNING) in ~30 ms — measured from the raw
//   weblog logs. So the QUEUED state is real but blinks past before the
//   dashboard can render it, and the counter reads "0 queued".
//
// What this does:
//   Capping maxForks makes same-process tasks (e.g. the two FASTQC lanes) run
//   one at a time. The second one then genuinely sits in the executor queue in
//   SUBMITTED state, so it shows as QUEUED on the dashboard until a slot frees.
//
// This trades throughput for visibility — it is a demo aid, not a default.
// Remove it (or raise maxForks) for a full-speed run.
process {
    maxForks = 1
}
